{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 83,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O God, keep not thou silence:\nHold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult;\nAnd they that hate thee have lifted up the head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They take crafty counsel against thy people,\nAnd consult together against thy hidden ones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from being a nation;\nThat the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they have consulted together with one consent;\nAgainst thee do they make a covenant:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites;\nMoab, and the Hagarenes;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek;\nPhilistia with the inhabitants of Tyre:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Assyria also is joined with them;\nThey have helped the children of Lot. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do thou unto them as unto Midian,\nAs to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the river Kishon;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who perished at Endor,\nWho became as dung for the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb;\nYea, all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who said, Let us take to ourselves in possession\nThe habitations of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my God, make them like the whirling dust;\nAs stubble before the wind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the fire that burneth the forest,\nAnd as the flame that setteth the mountains on fire,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So pursue them with thy tempest,\nAnd terrify them with thy storm.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fill their faces with confusion,\nThat they may seek thy name, O Jehovah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be put to shame and dismayed for ever;\nYea, let them be confounded and perish;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.83.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.83.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may know that thou alone, whose name is Jehovah,\nArt the Most High over all the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "God implored to confound his enemies.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "A Song, a Psalm of Asaph.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
